{
 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "intro",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# 03 - Data Transformation\n",
    "\n",
    "In this notebook we transform the cleaned datasets into a single **analytical fact table** (`fact_sales`) and a set of derived business tables.\n",
    "\n",
    "The fact table is the foundation for:\n",
    "- EDA (`04_eda.ipynb`)\n",
    - Business analysis (`05_business_analysis.ipynb`)\n",
    - The interactive dashboard (`dashboard/app.py`)\n",
    "\n",
    "We use `pandas.merge`, `groupby`, `pivot_table`, and conditional logic to produce:\n",
    "\n",
    "- **Operational metrics**: revenue, cost, profit, profit margin, discount amount.\n",
    "- **Customer metrics**: orders, units, frequency, recency, CLV.\n",
    "- **Time dimensions**: year, month, year-month, quarter for trend analysis.\n",
    "- **Aggregated views**: monthly, by category, by region, by channel, top products."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "setup",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import sys\n",
    "from pathlib import Path\n",
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "\n",
    "ROOT = Path('..').resolve()\n",
    "sys.path.insert(0, str(ROOT))\n",
    "\n",
    "PROC = ROOT / 'data' / 'processed'\n",
    "FINAL = ROOT / 'data' / 'final'\n",
    "FINAL.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n",
    "\n",
    "customers = pd.read_csv(PROC / 'customers.csv', parse_dates=['signup_date'])\n",
    "products  = pd.read_csv(PROC / 'products.csv', parse_dates=['launch_date'])\n",
    "orders    = pd.read_csv(PROC / 'orders.csv', parse_dates=['order_date'])\n",
    "items     = pd.read_csv(PROC / 'order_items.csv')\n",
    "returns   = pd.read_csv(PROC / 'returns.csv', parse_dates=['return_date'])\n",
    "\n",
    "from src.transformation import build_fact_sales\n",
    "fact = build_fact_sales(orders, items, products, customers, returns)\n",
    "print('Fact shape:', fact.shape)\n",
    "print('Columns:')\n",
    "for c in fact.columns:\n",
    "    print(' ', c)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "preview",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Spot-check the metrics"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "preview-fact",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "fact.head(3).T"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "verify-metrics",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "completed = fact[fact['is_completed']]\n",
    "print(f'Rows:                 {len(fact):,}')\n",
    "print(f'Completed orders:     {completed[\"order_id\"].nunique():,}')\n",
    "print(f'Revenue:              ${completed[\"net_revenue\"].sum():,.2f}')\n",
    "print(f'Cost:                 ${completed[\"cost\"].sum():,.2f}')\n",
    "print(f'Profit:               ${completed[\"profit\"].sum():,.2f}')\n",
    "print(f'Profit margin:        {completed[\"profit\"].sum() / completed[\"net_revenue\"].sum():.1%}')\n",
    "print(f'Return rate (items):  {completed[\"returned_flag\"].mean():.2%}')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "aggregations",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Aggregations used downstream"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "agg-fns",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from src.transformation import (\n",
    "    aggregate_monthly, aggregate_by_category, aggregate_by_region,\n",
    "    aggregate_by_channel, top_products, slow_moving_products,\n",
    "    customer_rfm, rfm_segment\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "monthly = aggregate_monthly(fact)\n",
    "by_cat  = aggregate_by_category(fact)\n",
    "by_reg  = aggregate_by_region(fact)\n",
    "by_ch   = aggregate_by_channel(fact)\n",
    "top20   = top_products(fact, n=20)\n",
    "slow    = slow_moving_products(fact, min_units=5)\n",
    "rfm     = rfm_segment(customer_rfm(fact))\n",
    "\n",
    "print('Monthly revenue:')\n",
    "display(monthly.tail(6))\n",
    "\n",
    "print('\\nBy category:')\n",
    "display(by_cat)\n",
    "\n",
    "print('\\nBy region:')\n",
    "display(by_reg)\n",
    "\n",
    "print('\\nBy channel:')\n",
    "display(by_ch)\n",
    "\n",
    "print('\\nTop 10 products by revenue:')\n",
    "display(top20.head(10))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "rfm",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## RFM segmentation\n",
    "\n",
    "Each customer is scored on Recency, Frequency and Monetary value using quartile binning, then assigned to a business-friendly segment."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "rfm-table",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "print('Segment distribution:')\n",
    "display(rfm['segment'].value_counts().to_frame('customers'))\n",
    "\n",
    "print('\\nSegment economics:')\n",
    "seg = (rfm.groupby('segment')\n",
    "         .agg(customers=('customer_id', 'count'),\n",
    "              avg_recency=('recency', 'mean'),\n",
    "              avg_frequency=('frequency', 'mean'),\n",
    "              avg_revenue=('revenue', 'mean'),\n",
    "              total_revenue=('revenue', 'sum'))\n",
    "         .round(2)\n",
    "         .sort_values('total_revenue', ascending=False))\n",
    "display(seg)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "save-final",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Persist the final analytical dataset\n",
    "\n",
    "We persist the **single fact table** plus a few pre-aggregated tables so the dashboard and downstream notebooks can read them quickly without re-running the full pipeline."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "save-final-2",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "fact.to_csv(FINAL / 'fact_sales.csv', index=False)\n",
    "monthly.to_csv(FINAL / 'monthly_summary.csv', index=False)\n",
    "by_cat.to_csv(FINAL / 'category_summary.csv', index=False)\n",
    "by_reg.to_csv(FINAL / 'region_summary.csv', index=False)\n",
    "by_ch.to_csv(FINAL / 'channel_summary.csv', index=False)\n",
    "top20.to_csv(FINAL / 'top_products.csv', index=False)\n",
    "rfm.to_csv(FINAL / 'rfm_segments.csv', index=False)\n",
    "\n",
    "print('Saved final tables to', FINAL)\n",
    "for f in FINAL.iterdir():\n",
    "    print(f'  - {f.name} ({f.stat().st_size // 1024} KB)')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "end",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Transformation recap\n",
    "\n",
    "We now have a star-style schema centered on `fact_sales`:\n",
    "\n",
    "- **One fact table** at line-item grain with revenue, cost, profit, discount, returns and time keys.\n",
    "- **Dimension aggregates**: monthly, by category, by region, by channel.\n",
    "- **RFM segmentation** for customer-level analysis.\n",
    "- **Top / slow-moving product** rankings.\n",
    "\n",
    "These outputs power the EDA and the dashboard that follow."
   ]
  }
 ],
